# Provenance for kb36_above_720p_2026-08-03.tsv
# (KB-36 — `speed >= 6 && is_1080p_or_larger -> default_min_partition_size =
#  BLOCK_8X8`, speed_features.c:311-313, was unmodelled.)

base commit      : e6f0e64 (origin/main after this session's first two landings)
host             : Darwin arm64 / Apple M4 Pro
profile          : test-fast (opt-level 3, debug-assertions + overflow-checks ON)
dispatch         : default (archmage SIMD tokens live); the change is a scalar
                   speed-feature assignment, and the same suite was run
                   AOM_FORCE_SCALAR=1
conformance dir  : AOM_CONFORMANCE_DIR=<primary checkout>/conformance/data

pristine arm     : an example binary over the same size x speed grid, run before
                   the one-hunk fix landed in
                   crates/aom-encode/src/speed_features.rs (8.5 min)
fixed arm        : the same binary after (8.5 min), plus the speed-8/9 rows from
                   cargo test --profile test-fast -p zenav1-aom-bench \
                     --test kb36_above_720p_speed_axis -- --ignored --nocapture

CONTENT
  mirror-tiled frame 0 of the conformance vector av1-1-b8-00-quantizer-00 (the
  kb22 / kb28 / kb31 / kb32 recipe), bd8 4:2:0, cq24 throughout.

THE FOUR SIZES
  1280x720   the ceiling `s4cov_hd_speed_axis.rs` reached and stopped at
  1920x1072  min dim 1072 — EIGHT pixels below `is_1080p_or_larger`
  1920x1080  min dim 1080 — ON it
  2560x1440  well above it

RESULT
  pristine  56 MATCH / 2 DIVERGE:
              1920x1080 cpu6  -127 B
              2560x1440 cpu6   +79 B
            Every other cell in the grid — including 1920x1072 at cpu6, the
            same content eight pixels shorter — is byte-exact. The window is
            exactly one speed wide: `set_allintra` sets the same field
            framesize-independently from speed 7 (speed_features.c:570), and
            below speed 6 the enclosing block does not run.
  fixed     32/32 MATCH, incl. speeds 8 and 9 at both >= 1080p sizes.

WHY NOTHING CAUGHT IT
  A speed sweep at any size below 1080 is green; a size sweep at any speed
  other than 6 is green. It needs the crossing. This is the SECOND arm on
  `default_min_partition_size`: KB-19 modelled `is_4k_or_larger` and its entry
  said the new method held "currently just the is_4k_or_larger one".
